#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-oilpaint.docbook:4
#, no-c-format
msgid "Oil Paint"
msgstr "Uljana slika"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-oilpaint.docbook:7
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &digikam; <emphasis>Oil Paint</emphasis> filter gives your image the "
"look of an oilpainting. It uses an algorithm copyrighted by Pieter Voloshyn."
msgstr ""
"&digikam; <emphasis>Uljana slika</emphasis> filter daje Vasoj slici izgled "
"uljanog crteza. Koristi algoritam koji je zastitio Pieter Voloshyn."

#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-oilpaint.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Uvod"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-oilpaint.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &digikam; <emphasis>Oil Paint</emphasis> filter gives your digital "
"images a nice oilpainting-like look. Images of nature and still lifes are "
"well suited for this effect."
msgstr ""
"&digikam; <emphasis>Uljana slika</emphasis> filter daje Vasoj digitalnoj "
"fotografiji izgled uljanog crteza.Slike prirode i zivota su pogodne za ovaj "
"efekat."

#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-oilpaint.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using the Oil Paint filter"
msgstr "Koristenje filtera Uljana slika"

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-oilpaint.docbook:25
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are two sliders to control the effect. The upper slider selects the "
"<guilabel>Brush Size</guilabel> between 1 and 5. Bigger brushes are better "
"suited for large images. <guilabel>Smooth</guilabel> controls the smoothness "
"or, seen from the other end, the jaggedness."
msgstr ""
"Postoje dva slajdera za kontrolu ovog efekta. Gornji slajder bira "
"<guilabel>Velicinu cetke</guilabel> izmedju 1 i 5. Vece cetke su bolje za "
"vece slike. <guilabel>Smeksaj</guilabel> kontrolise mekocu."

#. Tag: title
#: editor-filters-oilpaint.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Oil Paint filter in action"
msgstr "Aktivan filter Uljana slika."

#. Tag: para
#: editor-filters-oilpaint.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is an example of the oil paint filter effect. The original image is (1) "
"and the transformed image is (2). <guilabel>Brush Size</guilabel> for this "
"640 pixel size image is 1, <guilabel>Smooth</guilabel> is 17."
msgstr ""
"Ovo je primjer efekta uljane slike. Originalna slika je (1) a transformisana "
"je (2). <guilabel>Velicina cetke</guilabel> za ovu velicinu slike, velicine "
"piksela 640 je 1. <guilabel>Smeksaj</guilabel> je 17."

#. Tag: phrase
#: editor-filters-oilpaint.docbook:44
#, no-c-format
msgid "Oil Paint Image Effect Preview"
msgstr "Prikaz efekta Uljana slika"

#~ msgid "Special Effects (Filters)"
#~ msgstr "Specijalni efekti(Filteri)"

#~ msgid "Simulate Infrared Film"
#~ msgstr "Simuliraj infracirveni film"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The &digikam; <emphasis>Infrared Film</emphasis> filter simulates "
#~ "traditional infrared film material."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "&digikam; <emphasis>Infracrveni Film</emphasis> filter simulira "
#~ "tradicionalni infracrveni film."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Simulating classical infrared film material (the effect is rendered in "
#~ "black and white) is an interesting alienation effect that is even "
#~ "stronger and more dramatic than pure black and white conversion. Contrast "
#~ "and an abstract touch are improved, which can underpin the expression of "
#~ "the photographer as an artist. It is like taking an image in black and "
#~ "white with a red filter on the camera lenses. Areas which reflect little "
#~ "red light, &eg; the sky, will show as low density, dark areas. Areas "
#~ "which are excellent reflectors of red light, e.g. most green foliage, "
#~ "will be high density areas. And snow landscapes are really dramatic."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Simuliranje klasicnog infracrvenog filma je interesantno odvajanje efekta "
#~ "koje je cak jace i dinamicnije nego cisto crnobijela konverzija. Kontrast "
#~ "i apstraktnost su poboljsani, sto moze doprinijeti izrazavanju fotografa "
#~ "kao umjetnika. To je kao crnobijelo  slikanje sa crvenim filterom na "
#~ "objektivu. Podrucja koja reflektuju malo crvenog svjetla  &eg; poput "
#~ "neba, ce se pokazati kao tamna podrucja. Podrucja koja su izvrsni "
#~ "reflektori crvene svjetlosti poput zelenog lisca ce biti jako svjetla. A "
#~ "pejzazi snijega su zaista dramaticni."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The algorithm is based on the method of the 'Simulate Infrared Film' "
#~ "tutorial of the GimpGuru.org web site available at <ulink url=\"http://"
#~ "www.gimpguru.org/Tutorials/SimulatedInfrared\">this url</ulink>. The "
#~ "filter tries to reproduce the famous Ilford(tm) SFX200 infrared film. "
#~ "This film has a sensitivity range of 200-800 ISO."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Algoritam je baziran na metodi  'Simulate Infrared Film tutorijal na "
#~ "GimpGuru.org web stranici dostupnoj na linku <ulink url=\"http://www."
#~ "gimpguru.org/Tutorials/SimulatedInfrared\">this url</ulink>. Ovaj filter "
#~ "pokusava reproducirati poznati Ilford(tm) SFX200 infracrveni fil. Ovaj "
#~ "film ima osjetljivost u rangu 200-800 ISO."

#~ msgid "Using the Infrared Filter"
#~ msgstr "Koristenje infracrvenog filtera"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The left part of the dialog window lets you select the region to be shown "
#~ "in the preview section. Move the red rectangle with the mouse around to "
#~ "show the effect on different parts of the image."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Lijevi dio dijaloskog prozora Vam omogucava da odaberete dio koji ce biti "
#~ "prikazan u pregledu. Pomaknite crveni pravougaonik misem da vidite efekat "
#~ "na razlicitm dijelovima slike."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The lower part provides the two controls, Film Grain and ISO sensitivity. "
#~ "Check the <guilabel>Add Film Grain</guilabel> box if you want to simulate "
#~ "the grainy texture of a high sensitivity film. The ISO-level slider "
#~ "modifies the amount of filmgrain added and the predominance of green "
#~ "color (chlorophyll in nature) in the conversion mixer. Green pastures "
#~ "will become white as snow! Try it out."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Donji dio omogucava dvije kontrole, zrnastost filma i ISO osjetljivost. "
#~ "Provjerite <guilabel>Dodajte zrnastost filma</guilabel> ako zelite "
#~ "simulirati zrnastu teksturu visoko osjetljivog filma. ISO-slajder nivoa "
#~ "modificira kolicinu dodane zrnastosti filma i prevelike dominancije "
#~ "zelene boje(hlorofil u prirodi) u mikseru konverzije. Zeleni pasnjaci ce "
#~ "postati bijeli kao snijeg.Probajte!."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Because the filter mixes color channels to reproduce infrared film (with "
#~ "emphasis on green channel), one can not simulate infrared effect from "
#~ "black and white original photograph, since the color information is "
#~ "missing."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Zbog toga sto filter mijesa kanale boje za reproduciranje infracrvenog "
#~ "filma(sa naglaskom na zeleni kanal), ne moze se simulirati infracrveni "
#~ "efekat iz crnobijele originalne fotografije, jer nedostaje informacija o "
#~ "bojama."

#~ msgid "The filter in action"
#~ msgstr "Aktivan filter"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "This is an example of the infrared film effect applied to a color image "
#~ "taken in New Zealand's landscapes. The original image is (1) and the "
#~ "converted image is (2). The film sensitivity used to simulate the "
#~ "infrared film is ISO-400. Higher ISO values will create a kind of aura in "
#~ "the highlights."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ovo je primjer efekta infracrvenog filma primjenjenog na sliku u koloru, "
#~ "uslikanog pejzaza u Novom  Zelandu. Originalna slika je (1), a "
#~ "konvertovana(2). Film je simulirao infracrveni film u ISO-400. Vise ISO "
#~ "vrijednosti kreiraju vrstu aure u naglsenim podrucjima."

#~ msgid "The Infrared filter in Action"
#~ msgstr "Aktivan filter infracrvenog filma"

#~ msgid "Film Grain"
#~ msgstr "Zrnastost filma"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The &digikam; <emphasis>Filmgrain</emphasis> filter reproduces "
#~ "traditional film grain techniques of high speed films."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "&digikam; <emphasis>Zrno fima</emphasis> filter reproducira tradicionalne "
#~ "tehnike zrnastosti filmova."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The &digikam; <emphasis>Filmgrain</emphasis> filter is an easy tool to "
#~ "produce film grain on your images as known from classical high speed film "
#~ "material as, for example, the famous B/W KodaK Tri-X. In order to "
#~ "increase film sensitivity, manufacturers employed larger silver grains in "
#~ "the photo emulsion."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "&digikam; <emphasis>Zrno filma</emphasis> filter je jednostavan alat za "
#~ "produciranje zrnastosti filma na Vasim slikama poznatim kao poznati B/W "
#~ "KodaK Tri-X. U cilju povecanja osjetljivosti gilma, proizvodjaci su "
#~ "primjenili velika srebrena zrna u emulziji slika."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The film grain effect gives your shot a particular mood or seems to "
#~ "transport it in time. The treated image acquires a timeless atmosphere, "
#~ "detached from every day life. If you want that gritty, art-house, street-"
#~ "photography grainy film look, especially in monochromatic photos, use "
#~ "this filter."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Efekat zrnastosti daje Vasoj fotografiji odredjeni stimung ili se "
#~ "transportuje na vrijeme. Tretirana slika zahtjeva bezvremenu atmosferu, "
#~ "odvojenu od svakodnevnice.Ako zelite tu sljunkoviti, umjetnicki zrnasti "
#~ "izgled filma, posebno u monohromatskim slikama,koristite ovaj filter."

#~ msgid "Using the Filmgrain filter"
#~ msgstr "Koristenje filtera zrnastosti"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "There is a slider calibrated in ISO-sensitivity to control the grain "
#~ "intensity and granularity. The default is set to ISO-2400, although "
#~ "higher values are often required. If you still want more grain, apply the "
#~ "filter several times."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Postoji slajder kalibriran u ISO osjetljivosti za kontrolu intenziteta "
#~ "zrna i granularnost. Podrazumijevani je ISO-2400, iako su vece "
#~ "vrijednosti obicno zahtjevane. Ako jos uvijek zelite vise zrnastosti, "
#~ "primjenite filter nekoliko puta."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "This is an example of the film grain effect applied on a black and white "
#~ "image. The original image is (1) and the corrected image is (2). The film "
#~ "sensitivity used for simulate the film graininess is ISO-1600."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ovo je primjer efekta zrnastosti primjenjenog na crnobijelu fotografiju. "
#~ "Originalna slika je (1), a korigovana (2). Osjetljivost filma koristena "
#~ "za simuliranje zrnastosti je ISP-1600."

#~ msgid "The Film Grain Filter in Action"
#~ msgstr "Aktivan filter Zrnastost filma"

#~ msgid "Charcoal Drawing"
#~ msgstr "Ugljeni crtez"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The &digikam; <emphasis>Charcoal</emphasis> is an effect filter that "
#~ "creates a charcoal sketch-like result."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "&digikam; <emphasis>Ugalj</emphasis> je filter efekat koji kreira ugljeni "
#~ "skec kao rezultat."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The &digikam; <emphasis>Charcoal</emphasis> filter uses the gradients of "
#~ "color and luminosity to produce a grey scale charcoal sketch. The lines "
#~ "defining the outline of the image are pronounced. Images with slowly "
#~ "changing gradients are not ideal for this effect. It is helpful to "
#~ "imagine what scene you would pick to do as a hand sketch yourself, in "
#~ "order to choose the image to start with."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "&digikam; <emphasis>Ugalj</emphasis> filter koristi nijanse boje i "
#~ "osvjetljenje za proizvodnju ugljenog crteza u sivim nijansama. Linije "
#~ "koje definiriaju vanjstinu slike su naglasene. Slike sa usporenim "
#~ "mijenjanjem gradienta nisu idealne za ovaj efekat.Kao pomoc mozete "
#~ "zamisliti kakav prizor biste odabrali da napravite rucno skec, kao sliku "
#~ "sa kojom cete zapoceti."

#~ msgid "Using the Charcoal filter"
#~ msgstr "Koristenje filtera Ugalj"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "There are two sliders to control the effect on a scale of 1-100. The "
#~ "upper slider selects the pencil size, whereas the second slider adjusts "
#~ "the contrast (smoothness)."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Postoje dva slajdera za kontrolu efekta na skali od 1-100. Gornji slajder "
#~ "selektuje velicinu olocke, dok drugi namjesta kontrast."

#~ msgid "The Charcoal filter in action"
#~ msgstr "Aktivan filter Ugalj"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "This is an example of the charcoal filter. The original image is (1) and "
#~ "the transformed image is (2). Default values of 30 and 10 where applied. "
#~ "The result can be improved by adjusting the luminosity levels."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ovo je primjer filtera Ugalj. Originalna slika je (1), dok je "
#~ "transformisana (2). Podrazumijevane vrijednosti 30 i 10 su primjenjene. "
#~ "Rezultat se moze poboljsati podesavanjem nivoa osvjetljenja."

#~ msgid "The Charcoal filter in Action"
#~ msgstr "Aktivan filter Ugalj"

#~ msgid "Emboss Image"
#~ msgstr "Klesanje slike"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The &digikam; <emphasis>Emboss</emphasis> filter sculptures your image "
#~ "into 3-D as if it were stamped into wax. It uses an algorithm copyrighted "
#~ "by Pieter Voloshyn."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "&digikam; <emphasis>Klesanje</emphasis> filter oblikuje Vasu sliku kao3-D "
#~ "kao da je odstampana u vosku.koristi algoritam koji je zastitio Pieter "
#~ "Voloshyn."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The &digikam; <emphasis>Emboss</emphasis> filter is a quick tool to "
#~ "render your images in a 3-D effect. It works particularly well on images "
#~ "with simple structure where color is not the most important content. The "
#~ "filter uses the difference between colors and luminosity to convert it "
#~ "into a grey, moon-like landscape lit from 10 o'clock."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "&digikam; <emphasis>Isklesi</emphasis> filterje brzi alat koji ce "
#~ "napraviti Vasu sliku u 3-D formatu. Posebno dobro radi na slikama sa "
#~ "jednostavnom strukturom gdje boja nije najvazniji dio sadrzaja.Filter "
#~ "koristi razliku izmedju boja i osvjetljenja za pretvaranje u sivu, "
#~ "mjesecevu svjetlost vidljivu od 10 sati."

#~ msgid "Using the Emboss filter"
#~ msgstr "Koristenje filtera Isklesi"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The <guilabel>Depth</guilabel> control allows to define the contrast of "
#~ "the filtering. A value of 30 (10%) is the standard."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Dubina</guilabel> kontrola dopusta definisanje kontrasta "
#~ "filtera. Standardna vrijednost je 30 (10%)."

#~ msgid "The Emboss filter in action"
#~ msgstr "Aktivan filter Isklesi"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "This is an example of the emboss filter. The original image is (1) and "
#~ "the transformed image is (2). The <guilabel>Depth</guilabel> applied is "
#~ "10%."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Ovo je primjer filtera isklesi. Originalna slika je (1) a transformisana "
#~ "je (2). <guilabel>Dubina</guilabel> je promjenja 10%."

#~ msgid "The Emboss filter in Action"
#~ msgstr "Aktivan filter Isklesi"

#~ msgid "Distortion FX"
#~ msgstr "Distorzija FX"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The &digikam; <emphasis>Distortion FX</emphasis> is a series of "
#~ "distorting effects for digital still images."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "&digikam; <emphasis>Distorzija FX</emphasis>je serija efekata distorzije "
#~ "za digitalne slike."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "With this filter set, you can transform an ordinary photograph into a "
#~ "work of art suitable for framing using distorting operations. It uses "
#~ "algorithms copyrighted by Pieter Voloshyn."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Sa ovim setom filtera mozete transformisati obicnu fotografiju u "
#~ "umjetnicko djelo vrijedno uokvirivanja koristeci samo operacije "
#~ "distorzije. Koristi algoritam koji je zastitio Pieter Voloshyn."

#~ msgid "Using the filter"
#~ msgstr "Koristenje filtera"

#~ msgid "These are the distorting effects available:"
#~ msgstr "Ovo su dostupni efekti distorzije:"

#~ msgid "Type"
#~ msgstr "Tip"

#~ msgid "Preview"
#~ msgstr "Prikaz"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Fish Eyes</guilabel>: warps the photograph around a 3D "
#~ "spherical shape to reproduce the common photograph 'Fish Eyes' effect."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Fish Eyes efekat</guilabel>: pravi fotograju u obliku za "
#~ "reprodukciju efekta 'Fish Eyes'."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Twirl</guilabel>: spins the photograph to produce a Twirl "
#~ "pattern."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Brzo okreni</guilabel>: Okrece fotografiju kako bi proizvela "
#~ "Twirl obrazac."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Cylinder Horizontal</guilabel>: warps the photograph around a "
#~ "horizontal cylinder."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Horizontalni cilindar</guilabel>: zamotava fotografiju oko "
#~ "horizontalnog cilindra."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Cylinder Vertical</guilabel>: warps the photograph around a "
#~ "vertical cylinder."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Vertikalni cilindar</guilabel>: zamotava fotografiju oko "
#~ "vertikalnog cilindra."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Cylinder H/V</guilabel>: warps the photograph around a 2 "
#~ "cylinders, vertical and horizontal."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Cilindar H/V</guilabel>:zamotava fotografiju oko 2 cilindra, "
#~ "vertikalnog i horizontalnog."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Caricature</guilabel>: distorts photograph with 'Fish Eyes' "
#~ "effect inverted."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Karikatura</guilabel>: distorzira fotografiju sa obrutim 'Fish "
#~ "Eyes' efektom."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Multiple Corners</guilabel>: splits the photograph like a "
#~ "multiple corners pattern."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Visestruki uglovi</guilabel>: dijeli fotografiju na vise uglova."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Waves Horizontal</guilabel>: distorts the photograph with "
#~ "horizontal waves."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Horizontalni talasi</guilabel>: distorzira fotografiju sa "
#~ "horizontalnim talasima."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Waves Vertical</guilabel>: distorts the photograph with "
#~ "vertical waves."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Vertikani talasi</guilabel>: distorzira fotografiju sa "
#~ "vertikalnim talasima."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Block Waves 1</guilabel>: divides the image into cells and "
#~ "makes it look as if it is being viewed through glass blocks."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Blok talasa 1</guilabel>: dijeli fotografiju u celije i i cini "
#~ "da izgleda kao da se gleda kroz dijelove stakla."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Block Waves 2</guilabel>: like Block Waves 1 but with another "
#~ "version of glass blocks distortion."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Blok talasa 2</guilabel>: poput bloka talasa 1 ali sa "
#~ "drugacijim nacinom distorzije stakla."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Circular Waves 1</guilabel>: distorts the photograph with "
#~ "circular waves."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Cirkularni talasi 1</guilabel>: distorzira fotografiju "
#~ "cirkularnim talasima."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Circular Waves 2</guilabel>: other variation of Circular Waves "
#~ "effect."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Cirkularni talasi 2</guilabel>: varijacija efekta Cirkularni "
#~ "talasi 1."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Polar Coordinates</guilabel>: converts the photograph from "
#~ "rectangular to polar coordinates."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Polarne Koordinate</guilabel>: konvertuje fotografiju iz "
#~ "pravougaonika u polarne koordinate."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Unpolar Coordinates</guilabel>: Polar Coordinate effect "
#~ "inverted."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Nepolarne Koordinate</guilabel>: Suprotan efekat efektu Polarne "
#~ "Koordinate."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Tiles</guilabel>: splits the photograph into square blocks and "
#~ "move them randomly inside the image."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Plocice</guilabel>:dijeli fotografiju u kvadrate i pomjera ih "
#~ "random unutar slike."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Some effects can take a long time to run and cause high CPU load. You can "
#~ "always abort an effect by pressing <guilabel>Abort</guilabel> button "
#~ "during preview rendering."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Neki efekti se mogu duze poretati zbog ucitavanja CPU. Uvijek mozete "
#~ "prekinuti efekat pritiskom na <guilabel>Zavrsi</guilabel> dugme tokom "
#~ "operacije prikaza."

#~ msgid "The Distortion filter in action"
#~ msgstr "Aktivan filter Distorzija"

#~ msgid "The Distortion FX dialog tool in action is available below."
#~ msgstr "Dijaloski alat Distorzija FX je dostupan ispod."

#~ msgid "The Distortion FX Dialog Tool Preview"
#~ msgstr "Prikaz dijaloskog alata Distorzija FX"

#~ msgid "Blur FX"
#~ msgstr "Zamagli FX"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "The &digikam; <emphasis>Blur FX</emphasis> is a series of blurring "
#~ "effects for digital still images."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "&digikam; <emphasis>Zamagli FX</emphasis> je serija efekata zamagljivanja "
#~ "za digitalne slike."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "With this filter set, you can transform an ordinary photograph into a "
#~ "work of art suitable for framing using blurring operations. It uses "
#~ "algorithms copyrighted by Pieter Voloshyn."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "Sa ovim setom filtera mozete transformisati obicnu fotografiju u "
#~ "umjetnicko djelo prigodno za uokvirivanje koristeci operacije "
#~ "zamagljivanja. Koristi algoritam kojeg je zastitio Pieter Voloshyn."

#~ msgid "Using the Blurfx"
#~ msgstr "Koristenje Blurfx"

#~ msgid "These are the blurring effects available:"
#~ msgstr "Ovo su dostupni alati za zamagljivanje:"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Zoom Blur</guilabel>: blurs the image along radial lines "
#~ "starting from a specified center point. This simulates the blur of a "
#~ "zooming camera, thereby giving the photograph a dynamic expression as "
#~ "often seen in sport photography."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Zoom magla</guilabel>: zamagljuje sliku duz radijalnih linija "
#~ "pocevsiod specificne centralne tacke.Ovo simulira zamagljivanje kamere "
#~ "pri zumiranju, dajuci fotografiji dinamicki izraz koji se cesto vidi u "
#~ "sportskim fotografijama."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Radial Blur</guilabel>: blurs the image by rotating the pixels "
#~ "around the specified center point. This simulates the blur of a rotating "
#~ "camera."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Radialno zamagljivanje</guilabel>: zamagljuje sliku rotirajuci "
#~ "piksele oko specificne centralne tacke.Ovo simulira maglu rotiranja "
#~ "kamere."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Far Blur</guilabel>: blurs the image to simulate the effect of "
#~ "an unfocused camera lens. The subject seems to recede into the background."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Zmagljivanje u daljini</guilabel>:zamagljuje sliku da bi "
#~ "simulirala efekat nefokusiranog objektiva kamere. Cini se da subjekat "
#~ "odstupa od pozadine."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Motion Blur</guilabel>: blurs the image by swishing the pixels "
#~ "horizontally. This simulates the blur of a linearly moving camera, i.e. "
#~ "like a shot taken from a car or train."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Zamagljivanje pokreta</guilabel>: Zamagljuje sliku mjenjajuci "
#~ "piksele horizontalno. Ovo simulira maglu linearnog kretanja kamere i.e. "
#~ "poput slike, uslikane iz auta."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Focus Blur</guilabel>: blurs the image corners to reproduce the "
#~ "astigmatism distortion of a lens."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Focus Blur</guilabel>:Zamagljuje uglove slike za reproduciranje "
#~ "astigmeticne distorzije objektiva."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Softener Blur</guilabel>: blurs the image softly in the darker "
#~ "tones and strongly in the high lights. This gives photographs a dreamy "
#~ "and glossy soft focus effect (Hamilton effect). It's ideal for creating "
#~ "romantic portraits, glamour photography, or adding a warm and subtle glow."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Smeksaj i zamagli</guilabel>: lagano zamagljuje sliku u tamnim "
#~ "tonovima a jace u svjetlim.Ovo daje fotografiji sneni i sjajni "
#~ "efekt(Hamiltonov efekat). Idealan za kreiranje romanticnih portreta, "
#~ "glamournih slika ili dodavanja topline i suptilnog sjaja."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Shake Blur</guilabel>: blurs the image by randomly moving the "
#~ "pixels simulating the blur of an arbitrarily moving camera."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Protresi i zamagli</guilabel>: zamagljuje sliku random "
#~ "pomjerajuci piksele simulirajuci maglu proizvoljnog pomjerajnja kamere."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Smart Blur</guilabel>: finds the edges of color in photograph "
#~ "and blurs them without muddying the rest of the image."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Zamagli pametno</guilabel>: pronalazi ivice boje u fotografiji "
#~ "i zamagljuje ih bez unistavanja ostatka slike."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Frost Glass</guilabel>: blurs the image by simulating randomly "
#~ "dispersing light filtering through hoarse frosted glass."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Zamagljeno staklo</guilabel>: zamagljuje sliku simulirajuci "
#~ "random distorzionu svjetlost filtriranu kroz zamagljeno staklo."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "<guilabel>Mosaic</guilabel>: blurs the image by dividing the photograph "
#~ "into rectangular cells and then recreates it by filling those cells with "
#~ "average pixel value."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "<guilabel>Mozaik</guilabel>: zamagljuje sliku tako sto je podijeli na "
#~ "celije pravougaonikathe a potom ponovno kreira puneci te celije "
#~ "prosjecnom vrijednosti piksela."

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Some effects can take a long time to run and cause high CPU load. You can "
#~ "always abort an effect by pressing the <guilabel>Abort</guilabel> button "
